cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  ehr2cdm: a deterministic converter from local EHR exports to OMOP CDM 5.4
  and MEDS, with row-level lineage and an executable correctness contract
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Xinye
    family-names: Yang
    email: yangxinye2001@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/Yangxinyee/ehr-to-omop-meds-agent
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0
abstract: >-
  ehr2cdm converts local hospital EHR extracts (delimited text and spreadsheets)
  into OMOP CDM 5.4 and MEDS. The two targets are derived independently from a
  single canonical layer rather than one from the other, every published row
  carries a link back to the source rows it came from, and thirty-four checks encode
  the properties a conversion must satisfy before it can be used as training
  data -- including the leakage failures that are invisible to schema validation.
  Where the data does not answer a question, the converter blocks and says so
  instead of substituting a default.
keywords:
  - OMOP CDM
  - MEDS
  - electronic health records
  - data provenance
  - ETL validation
  - clinical machine learning
